Before a GitHub job likely to make more than about 100 REST calls, run `gh api rate_limit`. During the job, check `X-RateLimit-Remaining` on each core REST response. Stop before starting or continuing the job if fewer than 1,000 core requests remain. Send at most 4 REST requests at a time. Leave at least a minute between status checks in a loop.

Prefer one GraphQL query per repository over REST calls for individual pull requests. Prefer local Git (`git fetch`, `git log`, and `git merge-base`) over REST for questions about commits, ancestry, or merge methods. Prefer conditional requests when rereading a resource. Send its `ETag` with `If-None-Match`, or use `If-Modified-Since`. An authenticated 304 response costs no primary quota.
